! A soft X-ray line in the FLASH régime, for the second machine the source filter's
! default is measured on (doc/startup-noise.md). It is not FLASH: it is a line with
! FLASH's scales, chosen so that the ratio of the two angles the filter's default is
! built from differs from the Aramis benchmark's. Each segment is 165 periods, so the
! wiggler has a whole number of them. The beam is ten times the emittance
! and five times the size, the wavelength a hundred times longer, and z_R/L_g falls
! from 41 to about 16, which moves the ratio of the mode angle to the rho angle from
! 1.13 to about 1.9.

parameter[geometry] = open
parameter[particle] = electron
parameter[e_tot] = 8.0333e8

beginning[beta_a] = 10.0
beginning[beta_b] = 10.0

UND: wiggler, l = 4.5045, l_period = 0.0273, field_calc = helical_model, &
     b_max = 0.35307, tracking_method = fel_averaged, mat6_calc_method = tracking

D1: drift, l = 0.6
D2: drift, l = 0.3
QF: quadrupole, l = 0.1, k1 = 2.5
QD: quadrupole, l = 0.1, k1 = -2.5

FODO: line = (UND, D1, QF, D2, UND, D1, QD, D2)
FLASHLINE: line = (6*FODO)
use, FLASHLINE
